# Rank 1735 / CVE-2024-46898: SHIRASAGI's public page controller resolved the
# request path to a file under the site's public directory and sent it, with no
# canonicalisation between the two (CWE-22). ApplicationController#request_path
# is the raw value:
#
#   def request_path
#     request.env["REQUEST_PATH"] || request.path
#   end
#
# and Cms::PublicFilter, mixed into Cms::PublicController, threads it through
# three before_action methods into the send:
#
#   def set_request_path
#     @cur_path ||= request_path
#     ...
#   end
#   def parse_path
#     @cur_main_path.sub!(/\/$/, "/index.html")
#     @file = File.join(@cur_site.path, @cur_main_path)
#   end
#   def x_sendfile(file = @file)
#     return unless Fs.file?(file)
#     ss_send_file(file, type: Fs.content_type(file), disposition: :inline)
#   end
#
# File.join keeps the `..` components, so a request path of
# `docs/../../../../<rails-root>/README.md` escapes the site directory and the
# file is served inline. The fixed revision 5ac4685d7e4330f949f13219069107fc5d768934 adds
# SS.request_path(request), which runs the path through
# `Addressable::URI.parse(...).normalize.request_uri` — normalisation resolves
# the dot segments, so the joined path stays under the site root — and routes
# every request.path use through it.
#
# Both ends are labelled: `request.env` is code.HttpInput (binding
# httpInput12) and `send_file` is code.FilePathAccess (binding filePathAccess143),
# so VYQL-PATH-001 needs only a taint path between them. Four independent Ruby
# frontend gaps sit on that path, and the first test below pins the resulting
# miss. None of the four is a binding problem.
#
# 1. `@cur_path ||= request_path` bind nothing. `operator_assignment`
#    in internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/ruby.go's rbConv.stmt accepted only
#    an `identifier` left side and dropped every other target kind to a bare
#    ExprStmt — the value is evaluated and bound to nothing, exactly the defect
#    the multiple-assignment case in the same switch documents. It now
#    accepts the same target kinds as the plain assignment case beside it, and
#    the fourth test pins the recovered flow. Ruby memoises with
#    `@x ||= expr` everywhere, so this is the widest of the four.
# 2. A receiverless, paren-less call names no callee the resolver can match.
#    `request_path` in Ruby is an `identifier` node, indistinguishable from a
#    local variable read without scope tracking, so no Call node exists and the
#    trace dead-ends at `analysis.function.return`. `self.request_path` does
#    produce a Call, but with path `?.request_path` — the `self` receiver is
#    dropped rather than substituted with the enclosing class, the same gap
#    PHP's `dotted()` fixed for `self::`/`static::`. `request_path()` (parens,
#    no receiver) resolves and carries taint, which is why the third test's
#    inlined form reports.
# 3. An instance variable written in one method is not read in another.
#    `@cur_main_path` is assigned in `set_request_path` and consumed in
#    `parse_path`; a two-method pair with nothing else on the path reports
#    nothing, while the same assignment and read inside one method reports.
#    Ruby has no field-sensitive interprocedural summary, and Rails controller
#    concerns are built almost entirely out of exactly this shape.
# 4. A defaulted parameter does not see its default. `def x_sendfile(file = @file)`
#    lowers the body with `file` unbound to `@file`.
#
# Gaps 2 to 4 are not mechanical: 2 needs scope tracking to tell a call from a
# variable read, 3 is a new interprocedural dataflow relation, 4 needs default
# substitution wired into parameter lowering. Fixing gap 1 alone does not make
# the real shape detectable — the first test still reports nothing — so this
# rank is recorded as an engine gap rather than a fix.
#
# Scanning app/controllers at the vulnerable revision (1184 Ruby files) gives
# 453 findings, 27 of them VYQL-PATH-001, none on concerns/cms/public_filter.rb
# or on ApplicationController#request_path. The same tree after the op-assign fix
# is still 453 with identical per-rule counts; the only change is that one
# VYQL-PATH-001's source attribution moves from an unrelated controller into the
# memoising file that actually feeds its sink.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap

test "rank1735: the request path joined onto the site directory and served inline"
  lang ruby
  file app/controllers/application_controller.rb
  code
  ```
  class ApplicationController < ActionController::Base
    private

    def request_path
      request.env["REQUEST_PATH"] || request.path
    end

    def ss_send_file(file_or_path, opts = {})
      send_file file_or_path, opts
    end
  end
  ```
  file app/controllers/concerns/cms/public_filter.rb
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  module Cms::PublicFilter
    extend ActiveSupport::Concern

    included do
      before_action :set_request_path
      before_action :parse_path
      before_action :x_sendfile
    end

    def set_request_path
      @cur_path ||= request_path
      @cur_main_path = @cur_path.dup
    end

    def parse_path
      @cur_path.sub!(/\/$/, "/index.html")
      @cur_main_path.sub!(/\/$/, "/index.html")
      @file = File.join(@cur_site.path, @cur_main_path)
    end

    def x_sendfile(file = @file)
      return unless Fs.file?(file)
      ss_send_file(file, type: Fs.content_type(file), disposition: :inline)
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1735: the path is normalised before it is joined onto the site directory"
  lang ruby
  file app/controllers/application_controller.rb
  code
  ```
  module SS
    def request_path(request)
      Addressable::URI.parse(request.env["REQUEST_PATH"] || request.path).normalize.request_uri
    end
  end

  class ApplicationController < ActionController::Base
    include SS

    private

    def request_path
      @request_path ||= SS.request_path(request)
    end

    def ss_send_file(file_or_path, opts = {})
      send_file file_or_path, opts
    end
  end
  ```
  file app/controllers/concerns/cms/public_filter.rb
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  module Cms::PublicFilter
    extend ActiveSupport::Concern

    included do
      before_action :set_request_path
      before_action :parse_path
      before_action :x_sendfile
    end

    def set_request_path
      @cur_path ||= request_path
      @cur_main_path = @cur_path.dup
    end

    def parse_path
      @cur_path.sub!(/\/$/, "/index.html")
      @cur_main_path.sub!(/\/$/, "/index.html")
      @file = File.join(@cur_site.path, @cur_main_path)
    end

    def x_sendfile(file = @file)
      return unless Fs.file?(file)
      ss_send_file(file, type: Fs.content_type(file), disposition: :inline)
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1735: the same join and send report once the request path is read inline"
  lang ruby
  file app/controllers/concerns/cms/public_filter.rb
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  module Cms::PublicFilter
    def index
      cur_path = request.env["REQUEST_PATH"] || request.path
      cur_main_path = cur_path.sub(/\/$/, "/index.html")
      file = File.join(@cur_site.path, cur_main_path)
      send_file file, type: "text/html", disposition: :inline
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1735: a memoised request path keeps its taint through the op-assign"
  lang ruby
  file app/controllers/cms/public_controller.rb
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  class Cms::PublicController < ApplicationController
    def index
      @cur_path ||= params[:path]
      send_file File.join(@cur_site.path, @cur_path), disposition: :inline
    end
  end
  ```
